window.DD_FULL = window.DD_FULL || {}; window.DD_FULL["sat-1"] = {"questions":[{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":"e","passage":"Nang yai, a form of Thai shadow theatre, uses large panels of carved leather that performers hold above their heads while they dance in front of a lit screen. Because a single panel can weigh several kilograms and a performance may last for hours, the dancers must be physically ______.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["ornate","fragile","hesitant","robust"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"The dancers carry heavy panels for hours, so they must be strong and able to endure: 'robust'. 'Fragile' is the opposite, 'hesitant' describes uncertainty rather than physical strength, and 'ornate' describes decoration, not a person's body.","th":"นักแสดงต้องถือแผ่นหนังหนักหลายกิโลกรัมเป็นเวลาหลายชั่วโมง จึงต้องแข็งแรงทนทาน คือ robust ส่วน fragile (เปราะบาง) มีความหมายตรงข้าม hesitant (ลังเล) ไม่เกี่ยวกับร่างกาย และ ornate (ประดับประดา) ใช้กับสิ่งของ ไม่ใช่ความแข็งแรงของคน"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":"e","passage":"Most comets that pass near Earth are too faint to be seen without a telescope. Every few years, however, a comet grows so bright that it is ______ even from brightly lit cities, and crowds gather on rooftops to look at it.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["distant","frozen","visible","silent"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The contrast with comets 'too faint to be seen' and the crowds who 'look at it' show that the bright comet can be seen: 'visible'. 'Distant', 'silent' and 'frozen' may describe comets, but none of them explains why people in cities can watch it.","th":"ข้อความเปรียบเทียบกับดาวหางที่ 'จางเกินกว่าจะมองเห็น' และบอกว่าผู้คนออกมาดู จึงต้องเป็น visible (มองเห็นได้) ส่วน distant (ไกล) silent (เงียบ) และ frozen (แข็งตัว) ไม่ได้อธิบายว่าทำไมคนในเมืองจึงมองเห็นดาวหางได้"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":"e","passage":"Bangkok was once known as the \"Venice of the East\" because so many of its residents travelled and traded along canals, called khlongs. During the twentieth century, many khlongs were filled in to make room for roads as the city grew. In recent years, several districts have begun cleaning and reopening sections of canal for boat services and to help drain water during heavy rain.","stem":"Which choice best describes the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To compare Bangkok's canals in detail with those of Venice","To argue that Bangkok should replace its roads with canals","To describe how the role of Bangkok's canals has changed over time","To explain how the boats used on Bangkok's canals are built"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The text moves from the past (canals as main routes), to the twentieth century (canals filled in), to the present (canals reopened), so it describes how their role has changed. It never argues for removing roads, mentions Venice only in a nickname, and says nothing about how boats are built.","th":"ข้อความเล่าจากอดีต (คลองเป็นเส้นทางหลัก) สู่ศตวรรษที่ 20 (คลองถูกถมเป็นถนน) และปัจจุบัน (เปิดคลองใหม่) จึงเป็นการอธิบายว่าบทบาทของคลองเปลี่ยนไปอย่างไร ข้อความไม่ได้เสนอให้รื้อถนน ไม่ได้เปรียบเทียบกับเวนิสอย่างละเอียด และไม่ได้พูดถึงการสร้างเรือ"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":"m","passage":"Historian Kanya Rattanakul argues that the reforms of King Chulalongkorn's government in the late nineteenth century were not a simple copy of European models. Siamese officials, she shows, were ______: they adopted foreign methods of administration that suited the kingdom's needs while rejecting many others.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["indifferent","selective","reckless","unanimous"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The colon explains the blank: officials kept some foreign methods and rejected others, which means they were 'selective'. 'Indifferent' would mean they did not care, 'reckless' would mean they acted without thought, and 'unanimous' (all agreeing) says nothing about choosing some methods and rejecting others.","th":"ส่วนหลังเครื่องหมาย : อธิบายว่าเจ้าหน้าที่เลือกรับบางวิธีและปฏิเสธบางวิธี จึงเป็น selective (เลือกสรร) ส่วน indifferent (ไม่สนใจ) reckless (สะเพร่า ไม่ไตร่ตรอง) ขัดกับการคัดเลือกอย่างรอบคอบ และ unanimous (เป็นเอกฉันท์) ไม่เกี่ยวกับการเลือก"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":"m","passage":"The following text is from a short story.\nPim had not visited her grandmother's house in Lampang for eleven years. The mango tree still leaned over the well, and the narrow path still curved past the spirit house. What struck Pim most, though, was the quiet: no traffic, no voices, only the slow creak of the wooden shutters in the wind.","stem":"As used in the text, what does the word \"struck\" most nearly mean?","choices":["cancelled","impressed","hit","defeated"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The quiet is something Pim notices strongly, so 'struck' means 'impressed' (made a strong impression on her). 'Hit' is the physical meaning, 'defeated' is the sense used in contests, and 'cancelled' is the sense of 'struck from a list'; none fits a feeling caused by silence.","th":"ความเงียบเป็นสิ่งที่ทำให้พิมรู้สึกสะดุดใจมากที่สุด struck ในที่นี้จึงหมายถึง impressed (สร้างความประทับใจ/สะดุดใจ) ส่วน hit (ตี) เป็นความหมายทางกายภาพ defeated (เอาชนะ) และ cancelled (ขีดฆ่าออก) เป็นความหมายอื่นของคำนี้ที่ไม่เข้ากับบริบท"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":"m","passage":"Hummingbirds use energy faster than almost any other animal of their size, and they must feed every few minutes during the day. At night, when they cannot feed, this might seem to put them at risk of running out of energy before dawn. The birds avoid this danger by entering torpor, a state in which their body temperature and heart rate drop sharply, greatly reducing the energy they burn while they rest.","stem":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It traces the history of a discovery and then predicts what scientists will learn next.","It describes an experiment on an animal and then points out a weakness in the method.","It identifies a challenge that an animal faces and then explains how the animal deals with it.","It presents two theories about an animal's behaviour and then rejects both of them."],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The text first sets up a problem (hummingbirds burn energy fast and cannot feed at night) and then gives the solution (torpor). No theories are rejected, no experiment or method is described, and there is no history of a discovery or prediction.","th":"ข้อความเริ่มด้วยปัญหา (นกฮัมมิงเบิร์ดใช้พลังงานเร็วและกินอาหารตอนกลางคืนไม่ได้) แล้วอธิบายวิธีแก้ (เข้าสู่ภาวะ torpor) ข้อความไม่ได้เสนอทฤษฎีสองแบบ ไม่ได้บรรยายการทดลองหรือจุดอ่อนของวิธีการ และไม่ได้เล่าประวัติการค้นพบหรือทำนายอนาคต"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"cs","skill":"cross-text","difficulty":"h","passage":"Text 1\nAngkor, the great Khmer capital, was largely abandoned by the fifteenth century. Some researchers argue that its vast network of canals and reservoirs was the city's weak point. Decades of unusually strong monsoons alternating with long droughts, they say, filled channels with sand and broke embankments, and once the water system failed, the farms that fed the city could no longer be watered. In this view, the collapse of the water network drove people away.\nText 2\nClimate stress at Angkor was real, but the city's decline also coincided with a shift in political power toward the south, near present-day Phnom Penh, where sea trade with China was growing. Elites who moved south to profit from this trade took labour and resources with them. A water network as large as Angkor's needed constant maintenance by thousands of workers. It is therefore possible that the canals decayed because people had already begun to leave, rather than the other way around.","stem":"Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the view presented in Text 1?","choices":["By arguing that Angkor never experienced unusually strong monsoons or long droughts","By suggesting that the failure of the water network may have been a result, rather than a cause, of people leaving Angkor","By claiming that sea trade was less important to the Khmer than farming around Angkor","By agreeing that the failure of the water network was the main reason people left Angkor"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"Text 1 says the water system failed first and drove people away. Text 2 suggests the order may be reversed: people moved south, so no one maintained the canals. Text 2 accepts that 'climate stress … was real', so it does not deny the monsoons and droughts; it does not simply agree with Text 1; and it treats sea trade as important, not less important.","th":"ข้อความที่ 1 บอกว่าระบบน้ำพังก่อนแล้วทำให้คนอพยพ ข้อความที่ 2 เสนอว่าลำดับอาจกลับกัน คือคนย้ายลงใต้ก่อนจึงไม่มีใครดูแลคลอง ผู้เขียนข้อความที่ 2 ยอมรับว่าความแปรปรวนของสภาพอากาศเกิดขึ้นจริง จึงไม่ได้ปฏิเสธเรื่องมรสุมและภัยแล้ง ไม่ได้เห็นด้วยทั้งหมดกับข้อความที่ 1 และมองว่าการค้าทางทะเลมีความสำคัญ"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"central-ideas","difficulty":"e","passage":"In northeastern Thailand, weavers make mudmee silk by tying and dyeing bundles of thread before any weaving begins. Because the pattern is fixed into the threads in advance, a weaver must plan the whole design before setting up the loom. A single mistake in tying can shift the pattern across the entire cloth, so experienced weavers often spend more time preparing threads than weaving.","stem":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","choices":["Making mudmee silk requires careful planning because the pattern is created before the cloth is woven.","Mudmee weavers usually work faster than weavers who use other techniques.","Northeastern Thailand produces more silk than any other region of the country.","Mudmee silk is made mainly for sale to buyers outside Thailand."],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Every sentence supports the idea that the pattern is set in the threads first, so the weaver must plan carefully. The text says weavers spend a long time preparing, not that they are faster, and it gives no information about exports or about which region produces the most silk.","th":"ทุกประโยคสนับสนุนว่าลวดลายถูกกำหนดในเส้นด้ายก่อนทอ ผู้ทอจึงต้องวางแผนอย่างรอบคอบ ข้อความบอกว่าผู้ทอใช้เวลาเตรียมด้ายนาน ไม่ได้บอกว่าทำงานเร็วกว่า และไม่ได้กล่าวถึงการส่งออกหรือภาคที่ผลิตไหมมากที่สุด"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"evidence-textual","difficulty":"e","passage":"Every evening, thousands of fireflies gather in the mangrove trees along a river in Samut Songkhram province, flashing in the dark. A team of ecologists has hypothesized that bright artificial light from riverside buildings reduces the number of fireflies that gather in nearby trees.","stem":"Which finding, if true, would most directly support the ecologists' hypothesis?","choices":["Tourist boats travelled along the river more often on weekends than on weekdays.","The number of fireflies was about the same in trees near lit buildings and in trees far from them.","Mangrove trees growing next to buildings were taller than those growing farther away.","Trees far from lit buildings hosted many more fireflies than trees of the same species growing next to lit buildings."],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"The hypothesis predicts fewer fireflies near artificial light. A finding that trees far from lit buildings had many more fireflies than similar trees near them fits that prediction. Equal numbers near and far would weaken the hypothesis, while boat traffic and tree height say nothing about light and firefly numbers.","th":"สมมติฐานคาดว่าแสงไฟจากอาคารทำให้หิ่งห้อยน้อยลง ผลที่ว่าต้นไม้ไกลจากอาคารมีหิ่งห้อยมากกว่าต้นไม้ชนิดเดียวกันใกล้อาคารจึงสนับสนุนโดยตรง ถ้าจำนวนเท่ากันจะทำให้สมมติฐานอ่อนลง ส่วนเรื่องเรือท่องเที่ยวและความสูงของต้นไม้ไม่เกี่ยวกับแสงและจำนวนหิ่งห้อย"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"evidence-quantitative","difficulty":"e","passage":"A student tested whether soaking rice seeds in water before planting affects how many of them sprout. She soaked four groups of 100 seeds for different lengths of time and counted the seeds that had germinated after one week. She concluded that soaking helps, but that a longer soak does not always lead to more germination, since ______","table":{"title":"Rice seeds germinated after one week (out of 100)","rows":[["Soaking time (hours)","Seeds germinated"],["0","54"],["12","71"],["24","88"],["48","83"]]},"stem":"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the statement?","choices":["the group soaked for 12 hours had more germinated seeds than the group soaked for 24 hours.","the group that was not soaked had the fewest germinated seeds of the four groups.","the group soaked for 48 hours had fewer germinated seeds than the group soaked for 24 hours.","every group had more than 80 germinated seeds after one week."],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"To show that a longer soak is not always better, the student needs a case where more soaking gave fewer sprouts: 48 hours gave 83, fewer than the 88 at 24 hours. The unsoaked group having the fewest is true but shows only that soaking helps. The 12-hour group (71) did not beat the 24-hour group, and not every group had more than 80 (54 and 71).","th":"ต้องหากรณีที่แช่นานขึ้นแต่งอกน้อยลง คือแช่ 48 ชั่วโมงงอก 83 เมล็ด น้อยกว่าแช่ 24 ชั่วโมงที่งอก 88 เมล็ด การที่กลุ่มไม่แช่งอกน้อยที่สุดเป็นจริงแต่แสดงเพียงว่าการแช่ช่วยได้ กลุ่ม 12 ชั่วโมง (71) ไม่ได้มากกว่ากลุ่ม 24 ชั่วโมง และไม่ใช่ทุกกลุ่มที่งอกเกิน 80 เมล็ด (54 และ 71)"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"central-ideas","difficulty":"m","passage":"The following text is from a short story.\nArun had practised the piece for months, but on the night of the recital his fingers felt like borrowed things. He played the opening bars too quickly, slowed down, and then lost his place altogether. In the silence, he looked up and saw his teacher in the second row, nodding calmly, as if a pause were simply part of the music. Arun took a breath, found the next note, and continued.","stem":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","choices":["A nervous performer recovers from a mistake, helped by his teacher's calm reaction.","A teacher interrupts a recital in order to correct a student's errors.","A student decides to stop playing music after a disappointing recital.","A musician performs a difficult piece perfectly despite feeling nervous."],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Arun is nervous, loses his place, sees his teacher's calm nod and then continues: he recovers with his teacher's help. He does not give up, the teacher only nods and never interrupts, and the performance is not perfect because he loses his place.","th":"อรุณตื่นเต้น เล่นผิดจนหลงตำแหน่ง แต่เห็นครูพยักหน้าอย่างสงบจึงตั้งสติและเล่นต่อได้ เขาไม่ได้เลิกเล่นดนตรี ครูไม่ได้ขัดจังหวะการแสดง และการแสดงก็ไม่ได้สมบูรณ์แบบเพราะเขาเล่นผิด"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"evidence-textual","difficulty":"m","passage":"\"Monsoon Letter\" is a poem in which the speaker writes to a friend about the rainy season. Throughout the poem, the speaker presents the rain as both an inconvenience and a source of comfort.","stem":"Which quotation from \"Monsoon Letter\" most effectively illustrates the claim?","choices":["\"I wait all day for sun that will not come; / my shoes are soaked, my letters left unsent.\"","\"The mango trees stand silent in the heat, / too tired to move before the storm arrives.\"","\"The rain has flooded every road I take, / and yet each night it sings me into sleep.\"","\"The clouds arrive like dancers from the sea, / and silver threads hang down from every roof.\""],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The claim has two parts: the rain is an inconvenience and a comfort. Only the lines about flooded roads (inconvenience) and the rain singing the speaker to sleep (comfort) show both. The clouds 'like dancers' only describe the rain, the soaked shoes show only the inconvenience, and the mango trees describe the heat before the rain.","th":"ข้ออ้างมีสองส่วน คือฝนเป็นทั้งความไม่สะดวกและความอบอุ่นใจ มีเพียงบทที่พูดถึงถนนน้ำท่วม (ไม่สะดวก) และฝนที่กล่อมให้หลับ (อบอุ่นใจ) ที่แสดงครบทั้งสองด้าน บทเรื่องเมฆเหมือนนักเต้นเป็นแค่การบรรยาย บทเรื่องรองเท้าเปียกแสดงแค่ความไม่สะดวก และบทเรื่องต้นมะม่วงพูดถึงความร้อนก่อนฝนตก"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"inferences","difficulty":"m","passage":"At an excavation site in northern Thailand, archaeologists found grains of rice in soil layers dated to about 3,000 years ago. The grains came from rice varieties typically grown in flooded paddy fields. Older layers at the same site contain grains only of varieties typically grown in dry, upland fields. These findings suggest that, around 3,000 years ago, the people living at the site ______","stem":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["began growing rice in flooded fields.","moved to a drier location in the mountains.","stopped growing rice altogether.","traded most of their rice to distant regions."],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Older layers show only dry-field rice, while layers from about 3,000 years ago show flooded-paddy rice, so people at the site most likely started wet-field farming then. They did not stop growing rice, since rice grains are still found; moving to a drier place conflicts with the new paddy rice; and nothing in the text concerns trade.","th":"ชั้นดินที่เก่ากว่ามีแต่ข้าวไร่ ส่วนชั้นอายุราว 3,000 ปีมีข้าวนาน้ำ จึงสรุปได้ว่าคนเริ่มปลูกข้าวในนาน้ำขังในช่วงนั้น พวกเขาไม่ได้เลิกปลูกข้าวเพราะยังพบเมล็ดข้าว การย้ายไปที่แห้งขัดกับการพบข้าวนาน้ำ และข้อความไม่ได้พูดถึงการค้าเลย"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"ii","skill":"inferences","difficulty":"h","passage":"An economist studying street-food vendors in Bangkok found that vendors who accept QR-code payments report higher daily sales than vendors who accept only cash. However, the vendors who accept QR codes were also much more likely to be located near office buildings, where customers tend to spend more per meal even when they pay in cash. Therefore, the higher sales reported by vendors who accept QR codes ______","stem":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["indicate that vendors near office buildings rarely accept cash payments.","may be explained at least partly by where those vendors are located rather than by the payment method itself.","show that office workers prefer to pay for street food in cash.","prove that offering QR-code payments causes customers to spend more on each meal."],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The text points out a second difference between the groups: location. Since customers near offices spend more even in cash, location could account for some of the higher sales. 'Prove that QR payments cause' ignores this problem; the text never says office workers prefer cash; and it says nothing about vendors near offices refusing cash.","th":"ข้อความชี้ว่าผู้ค้าที่รับ QR มักอยู่ใกล้อาคารสำนักงานซึ่งลูกค้าจ่ายมากกว่าแม้จ่ายเงินสด ยอดขายที่สูงกว่าจึงอาจเกิดจากทำเลมากกว่าวิธีชำระเงิน การบอกว่า 'พิสูจน์ว่า QR ทำให้ลูกค้าจ่ายมากขึ้น' ละเลยปัญหานี้ ข้อความไม่ได้บอกว่าพนักงานออฟฟิศชอบเงินสด และไม่ได้บอกว่าผู้ค้าใกล้สำนักงานไม่รับเงินสด"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"sec","skill":"boundaries","difficulty":"e","passage":"Plants that live in deserts have developed different ways to survive long periods without rain. Many store water in their thick ______ send roots deep underground to reach moisture that lies far below the surface.","stem":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["stems, and, others","stems others","stems. Others","stems, others"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"'Many store water in their thick stems' and 'Others send roots deep underground' are both complete sentences, so a period between them is correct. A comma alone creates a comma splice, no punctuation creates a run-on sentence, and the comma after 'and' wrongly separates the conjunction from the clause it introduces.","th":"'Many store water in their thick stems' และ 'Others send roots…' เป็นประโยคสมบูรณ์ทั้งคู่ จึงต้องแยกด้วยจุด การใช้จุลภาคอย่างเดียวเป็น comma splice การไม่ใส่เครื่องหมายเลยทำให้เป็นประโยคต่อกันผิดหลัก และการใส่จุลภาคหลัง and เป็นการแยกคำเชื่อมออกจากอนุประโยคโดยไม่จำเป็น"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"sec","skill":"form-structure-sense","difficulty":"e","passage":"Last year, the students in Ms. Lin's science class ______ a small weather station on the roof of their school. They still check its readings every morning and post the results on a board outside the classroom.","stem":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["built","are building","will build","build"],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"'Last year' places the action in the past, so the past tense 'built' is needed. 'Build' and 'are building' are present forms, and 'will build' refers to the future; all of these conflict with 'last year' and with the fact that the station already exists.","th":"'Last year' บอกว่าเหตุการณ์เกิดในอดีต จึงต้องใช้ built (อดีต) ส่วน build และ are building เป็นรูปปัจจุบัน will build เป็นอนาคต ซึ่งขัดกับ last year และกับข้อเท็จจริงว่าสถานีมีอยู่แล้ว"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"sec","skill":"boundaries","difficulty":"m","passage":"Many visitors who travel north from Bangkok stop at the historical park in the town of Sukhothai. The ancient city of ______ was the capital of an early Thai kingdom in the thirteenth century, now attracts thousands of tourists every year.","stem":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["Sukhothai; which","Sukhothai, which","Sukhothai which","Sukhothai: which"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The clause 'which was the capital … century' adds extra information about Sukhothai and is already closed by a comma after 'century', so it must also be opened by a comma: 'Sukhothai, which'. Leaving out the comma breaks the pair, and a semicolon or a colon cannot separate a subject from the rest of its own sentence.","th":"อนุประโยค which was the capital … century เป็นข้อมูลเสริม และมีจุลภาคปิดท้ายหลัง century แล้ว จึงต้องมีจุลภาคเปิดหน้าด้วย คือ Sukhothai, which การไม่ใส่จุลภาคทำให้ไม่เป็นคู่ ส่วน ; และ : ไม่สามารถใช้แยกประธานออกจากส่วนที่เหลือของประโยคเดียวกันได้"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"sec","skill":"boundaries","difficulty":"m","passage":"Early European maps of the Gulf of Thailand often placed rivers and islands in the wrong ______ sailors continued to rely on them for many years because no better charts of the region were available.","stem":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["positions, nevertheless,","positions nevertheless","positions, nevertheless;","positions; nevertheless,"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"Two independent clauses are joined here with the adverb 'nevertheless'. The correct pattern is a semicolon before the adverb and a comma after it: 'positions; nevertheless,'. Commas on both sides create a comma splice, no punctuation creates a run-on, and putting the semicolon after 'nevertheless' attaches the adverb to the wrong clause.","th":"มีอนุประโยคอิสระสองประโยคเชื่อมด้วยคำวิเศษณ์ nevertheless รูปแบบที่ถูกคือ ; หน้าคำ และ , หลังคำ การใช้จุลภาคทั้งสองข้างเป็น comma splice การไม่ใส่เครื่องหมายเป็นประโยคต่อกันผิดหลัก และการวาง ; หลัง nevertheless ทำให้คำนี้ไปอยู่ผิดอนุประโยค"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"sec","skill":"form-structure-sense","difficulty":"m","passage":"Poison dart frogs of Central and South America are among the most brightly coloured animals on Earth. The vivid colours of the frog's skin ______ predators that the animal is toxic and should not be eaten.","stem":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["has warned","warns","warn","is warning"],"answer":2,"explanation":{"en":"The subject of the verb is 'colours' (plural), not 'skin' or 'frog', so the plural verb 'warn' is needed. 'Warns', 'has warned' and 'is warning' are all singular forms that would agree only with a singular subject.","th":"ประธานของกริยาคือ colours (พหูพจน์) ไม่ใช่ skin หรือ frog จึงต้องใช้ warn ส่วน warns, has warned และ is warning เป็นรูปเอกพจน์ ใช้กับประธานเอกพจน์เท่านั้น"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"sec","skill":"boundaries","difficulty":"h","passage":"Composer Narong Sirisak has written music for film, dance, and theatre. His most ambitious work—a suite for the ranat ek, a Thai xylophone, and a full string ______ was first performed in Bangkok in 2011 and has since been recorded by orchestras in three countries.","stem":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["orchestra","orchestra;","orchestra,","orchestra—"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"The description of the work begins with a dash after 'work', so it must end with a matching dash: 'orchestra—'. A comma does not close a phrase opened by a dash, a semicolon cannot separate the subject 'work' from its verb 'was', and leaving out the punctuation leaves the dash unpaired.","th":"ข้อความที่อธิบายผลงานเปิดด้วยขีดยาว (—) หลัง work จึงต้องปิดด้วยขีดยาวเช่นกัน คือ orchestra— การใช้จุลภาคไม่สามารถปิดวลีที่เปิดด้วยขีดยาวได้ ; ไม่สามารถแยกประธาน work ออกจากกริยา was ได้ และการไม่ใส่เครื่องหมายทำให้ขีดยาวไม่ครบคู่"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"sec","skill":"form-structure-sense","difficulty":"h","passage":"Gibbons living in the forests of Khao Yai National Park sing loud, complex songs at dawn, and each animal's song is slightly different. Having spent two decades recording these songs, ______","stem":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["biologist Somsak Prasert can identify individual gibbons by their calls alone.","individual gibbons can be identified by biologist Somsak Prasert by their calls alone.","the calls of individual gibbons can be identified alone by biologist Somsak Prasert.","biologist Somsak Prasert's ability to identify individual gibbons by their calls alone is remarkable."],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"The phrase 'Having spent two decades recording these songs' must be followed by the person who did the recording. Only the version that begins with 'biologist Somsak Prasert' does this. The others make 'individual gibbons', 'the calls' or 'Somsak Prasert's ability' the subject, as if they had spent two decades recording songs.","th":"วลี Having spent two decades recording these songs ต้องตามด้วยผู้ที่ทำการบันทึกเสียง คือ biologist Somsak Prasert ตัวเลือกอื่นขึ้นต้นด้วย individual gibbons, the calls หรือ Somsak Prasert's ability ทำให้ความหมายผิดเหมือนว่าชะนี เสียงร้อง หรือความสามารถเป็นผู้บันทึกเสียงมา 20 ปี (dangling modifier)"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"eoi","skill":"transitions","difficulty":"e","passage":"Durian, a fruit grown widely in Thailand and Malaysia, is famous for its powerful smell, which many people find unpleasant. ______ a number of hotels and train services in the region do not allow passengers or guests to bring durian inside.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["In contrast,","For instance,","Similarly,","As a result,"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"The ban on durian is a consequence of its strong smell, so 'As a result' is the logical transition. 'In contrast' signals an opposing idea, 'Similarly' signals a comparable point, and 'For instance' introduces an example, but the second sentence is an effect of the first.","th":"การห้ามนำทุเรียนเข้าโรงแรมและรถไฟเป็นผลมาจากกลิ่นแรง จึงใช้ As a result ส่วน In contrast ใช้กับความขัดแย้ง Similarly ใช้กับสิ่งที่คล้ายกัน และ For instance ใช้ยกตัวอย่าง ซึ่งไม่ตรงกับความสัมพันธ์แบบเหตุและผล"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"eoi","skill":"rhetorical-synthesis","difficulty":"e","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- The Thai alphabet has 44 consonant letters.\n- It developed from the Old Khmer script.\n- Tradition holds that it was created in 1283 under King Ramkhamhaeng of Sukhothai.\n- Thai is written from left to right.\n- Spaces in written Thai usually mark the ends of phrases or sentences, not the gaps between words.","stem":"The student wants to describe the origins of the Thai alphabet. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Thai alphabet developed from the Old Khmer script, and tradition holds that it was created in 1283 under King Ramkhamhaeng.","The Thai alphabet, which has 44 consonant letters, is written from left to right.","In written Thai, spaces usually mark the ends of phrases or sentences.","Thai is written from left to right, and spaces do not usually appear between words."],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"Only the sentence about the Old Khmer script and the traditional date of 1283 explains where the alphabet came from. The other sentences describe how Thai looks or is written today (number of letters, direction, spacing), not its origins.","th":"มีเพียงประโยคที่กล่าวถึงอักษรขอมโบราณและปี 1283 สมัยพ่อขุนรามคำแหงที่อธิบายที่มาของอักษรไทย ประโยคอื่นบอกลักษณะการเขียนในปัจจุบัน (จำนวนพยัญชนะ ทิศทางการเขียน การเว้นวรรค) ไม่ใช่ที่มา"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"eoi","skill":"transitions","difficulty":"m","passage":"Many people assume that the Mekong giant catfish, one of the largest freshwater fish in the world, must be a fierce hunter. ______ adults of the species have no teeth and feed mainly on algae and other plant material.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["For this reason,","In reality,","Likewise,","Therefore,"],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"The second sentence corrects the common assumption in the first, so 'In reality' fits. 'Therefore' and 'For this reason' would present the fish's diet as a result of people's assumption, and 'Likewise' would suggest the two sentences make similar points.","th":"ประโยคที่สองแก้ความเชื่อผิดในประโยคแรก จึงใช้ In reality ส่วน Therefore และ For this reason ทำให้ดูเหมือนอาหารของปลาเป็นผลจากความเชื่อของคน และ Likewise ใช้กับสิ่งที่คล้ายกัน"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"eoi","skill":"transitions","difficulty":"m","passage":"Traditional Thai houses were often built on tall wooden stilts, which kept the living areas above the water during the rainy-season floods. ______ the raised floors allowed cool air to move beneath the house, making the rooms more comfortable during the hot season.","stem":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["In other words,","Instead,","Nevertheless,","Moreover,"],"answer":3,"explanation":{"en":"The second sentence adds a second benefit of building on stilts, so 'Moreover' is correct. 'Nevertheless' signals a contrast, 'Instead' signals a replacement, and 'In other words' signals a restatement, but cooler rooms is a new advantage, not a restatement of flood protection.","th":"ประโยคที่สองเพิ่มข้อดีอีกข้อของบ้านใต้ถุนสูง จึงใช้ Moreover ส่วน Nevertheless แสดงความขัดแย้ง Instead แสดงการแทนที่ และ In other words ใช้กล่าวซ้ำด้วยคำอื่น แต่ความเย็นเป็นข้อดีใหม่ ไม่ใช่การกล่าวซ้ำเรื่องน้ำท่วม"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"eoi","skill":"rhetorical-synthesis","difficulty":"m","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- Corrado Feroci was an Italian sculptor born in Florence in 1892.\n- He moved to Siam (now Thailand) in 1923 to work for the government.\n- He later took the Thai name Silpa Bhirasri.\n- In 1943, he founded the school that became Silpakorn University.\n- He is often called the father of modern Thai art.","stem":"The student wants to emphasize Silpa Bhirasri's influence on art education in Thailand. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Corrado Feroci, an Italian sculptor, is also known by his Thai name, Silpa Bhirasri.","Silpa Bhirasri, often called the father of modern Thai art, founded the school that became Silpakorn University in 1943.","Born in Florence in 1892, Corrado Feroci later took the Thai name Silpa Bhirasri.","In 1923, Italian sculptor Corrado Feroci moved to Siam to work for the government."],"answer":1,"explanation":{"en":"Founding the school that became Silpakorn University is the note about art education, and calling him the father of modern Thai art stresses his influence. The other sentences give his birthplace, his Thai name or his move to Siam, which do not show any influence on education.","th":"การก่อตั้งโรงเรียนที่กลายเป็นมหาวิทยาลัยศิลปากรคือข้อมูลเรื่องการศึกษาศิลปะ และฉายา 'บิดาแห่งศิลปะไทยสมัยใหม่' เน้นอิทธิพลของเขา ประโยคอื่นบอกเพียงบ้านเกิด ชื่อไทย หรือการย้ายมาสยาม ซึ่งไม่ได้แสดงอิทธิพลต่อการศึกษา"}},{"kind":"sat","domain":"eoi","skill":"rhetorical-synthesis","difficulty":"h","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- A lichen is made of a fungus living together with an alga or a cyanobacterium.\n- The fungus provides structure and protection.\n- The alga or cyanobacterium makes food through photosynthesis.\n- Many kinds of lichens are very sensitive to air pollution.\n- Scientists can use the number and types of lichens growing on trees to estimate a city's air quality.","stem":"The student wants to explain to an audience unfamiliar with lichens why scientists study them in cities. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because many lichens—organisms formed by a fungus living with an alga or a cyanobacterium—are very sensitive to air pollution, scientists can use them to estimate a city's air quality.","In a lichen, the fungus provides structure, while the alga or cyanobacterium makes food through photosynthesis.","Lichens, which are made of a fungus and an alga or a cyanobacterium, grow on trees in many cities.","Scientists can use the number and types of lichens growing on trees to estimate a city's air quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":{"en":"The goal has two parts: the audience does not know what lichens are, and the sentence must say why scientists study them in cities. Only the sentence that defines a lichen and links its sensitivity to pollution with measuring air quality does both. The sentence about estimating air quality does not define lichens or explain why they work; the sentence about the fungus and alga never mentions cities or pollution; and the sentence about lichens growing on trees gives no reason for studying them.","th":"เป้าหมายมีสองส่วน คือผู้อ่านไม่รู้จักไลเคน และต้องบอกเหตุผลที่นักวิทยาศาสตร์ศึกษาไลเคนในเมือง ประโยคที่ถูกทั้งอธิบายว่าไลเคนคืออะไรและเชื่อมความไวต่อมลพิษกับการวัดคุณภาพอากาศ ประโยคเรื่องการประเมินคุณภาพอากาศไม่ได้อธิบายว่าไลเคนคืออะไรหรือทำไมใช้ได้ ประโยคเรื่องรากับสาหร่ายไม่พูดถึงเมืองหรือมลพิษ และประโยคเรื่องไลเคนขึ้นบนต้นไม้ไม่ได้ให้เหตุผลในการศึกษา"}}]};
